                        "entry_id": "8bebb3bb-a776-3483-aa1f-14f4d5e31b00",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A space left unroofed over the court of a dwelling in Ancient Rome, through which the rain fell into the impluvium or cistern."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8de8e7ae-438d-4573-96d3-710c1660960a",
                                "sense_id": "e2fe4119-65be-3a9c-b7d7-24396a24ecf0",
                                "text": "In the centre of the floor of the atrium a portion was sunk for the reception of rain water; this was termed the impluvium; and above it an opening of similar dimensions was left in the ceiling or roof, termed the compluvium."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
